  "term": "neurohormone",
  "definition": "A neurohormone is a hormone-like signaling substance, such as GnRH, that controls body functions by acting on specific receptors in target cells. In the supplied source, GnRH is the neurohormone that helps regulate reproductive function through pituitary gonadotrope cells.",
